# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# FILLMODE (register 0x110) mode fixture, built from live capture
# irix-20260922T055519-8b72de (QEMU 4ddb0e1ce4 at capture time). Every
# 'write 8 0x120400' word below is the guest's own 64-bit command word,
# copied from qemu.trace by line number, not re-encoded.
#
# The wid assertions below are all zero: no CHAR_H/CHAR_L execute writes
# the WID plane, which only a rectangle fill with a nonzero COLORMASKMSBS
# does (see cmap-xmap-wid.replay). They fail on a model that tags a pixel
# from the operation that painted it.
#
# FILLMODE == 0x10c00000 selects byte-pixel transfer mode: one CHAR_L
# execute (CHAR_H is staged first and never itself executes) delivers
# eight 8-bit indexed pixels of the current row, CHAR_H bytes MSB to LSB
# then CHAR_L bytes MSB to LSB, left to right. The row advances after
# ceil((skip + w) / 8) executes, where skip = (row * 4 * ceil(w / 4)) mod 8
# is the source scanline's offset from an 8-byte boundary (approximated;
# the register that would state this directly is unidentified, see
# hw/misc/sgi-mgras-raster.c).
#
# FILLMODE == 0x10400008 selects bitmap glyph mode: one execute on either
# CHAR_H or CHAR_L paints one row of up to 64 columns, CHAR_H bits 31..0
# as columns 0-31 and CHAR_L bits 31..0 as columns 32-63, MSB first; a set
# bit paints PACKEDCOLOR direct (WID 0), a clear bit paints BKGRD_RG
# indexed (WID DRBPOINTERS>>16); the row counter advances by one per
# execute.
#
# This fixture was written without running QEMU. It is expected to FAIL
# on trunk (no CHAR_L paint) and to PASS once hw/misc/sgi-mgras-raster.c
# implements both FILLMODE modes above.

# --- command-channel handshake, copied from tests/data/mgras/fill.replay ---
